{
  "requirement": "For requirement and example evidence, both `true` and `FIXME` MUST satisfy the determination check in `habeas::validate()`. A false determination MUST fail validation and be reported with its rationale. Each definition's determination MUST be checked on its own; a false determination MUST NOT fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. All other evidence checks MUST still pass: FIXME MUST NOT excuse malformed, missing, or stale evidence or uncovered references. Validation MUST check the recorded outcome, schema, input freshness, and reference coverage without inference or reassessing whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no unacknowledged gap in code, marking or tests.\n\n**Obligations and the code that carries them out**\n\n1. **`true` and FIXME satisfy the determination check.**\n   - `validate_evidence_file` (src/evidence.rs, marked `{impl}` determination) parses the judgment with `Judgment::from_value`.\n   - It adds an error only for `Judgment::False`, so `true` and FIXME records add none.\n   - FIXME strings are checked separately against the `{fixme}` references, in `validate_fixme_entries` called from `validate_references`. That is a check of the recorded outcome and does not reassess the gap, as the requirement allows. It carries `{impl}` for ci.outcomes, which covers it.\n2. **A false determination fails validation and reports its rationale.**\n   - The same function pushes `\"{label}: determination is false: <trimmed rationale>\"`.\n   - src/citations.rs `validate` is also marked `{impl}` determination. The false check it relies on is in `validate_review`.\n3. **Each definition is checked on its own.**\n   - The check runs per evidence file, with no cross-definition logic, so a false record cannot fail the definitions it implements, tests or cites.\n4. **FIXME does not excuse malformed, missing or stale evidence, or uncovered references.**\n   - Schema checks, missing-evidence errors, stale-input checks and the \"no input covers\" check never look at FIXME. These are in `validate_evidence_file`, `inspect_repository_with_progress` and `validate_references`.\n5. **No inference or reassessment.**\n   - The checks are mechanical comparisons of recorded fields with current sources.\n   - The FIXME entry check compares strings only.\n\n**Tests, all marked `{test}` for this requirement**\n\n- **True and FIXME pass:** `fixme_fixture` in tests/commands.rs, `fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not`, and the batch tests in tests/authoring_batch.rs.\n- **False fails with its rationale:**\n  - src/evidence.rs `a_false_determination_fails_only_its_own_record_with_its_rationale` asserts the exact error text, including the trimmed rationale.\n  - `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` and `an_unacknowledged_gap_beside_an_acknowledged_one_is_false` also check it.\n- **Independence from definitions it implements or cites:** `a_false_determination_fails_only_its_own_record_with_its_rationale` asserts that the only error is the false record's own, with the other record valid and linked by `{impl}` and `{cite}`.\n- **FIXME does not hide stale inputs or uncovered references:** `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` checks the \"outline input changed\" and \"no input covers\" errors on a FIXME record.\n- **Malformed FIXME:** `malformed_fixme_is_invalid_and_reports_the_required_shape` is untagged for this requirement but is not needed to cover it. The FIXME-specific schema checks and the issue-matching rules have their own requirements and tests.\n- **Missing evidence:** `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` and others assert \"missing for requirement\". The code has no FIXME conditional, so no separate FIXME-plus-missing test is needed.\n\n**Marking and unspecified behavior**\n\nI found no code implementing part of this requirement without an `{impl}` reference, and no unmarked test of it. I found no unspecified observable behavior in the `{impl}` code. The citation-review rejection of FIXME belongs to the citation-review requirement, not this one.\n\nNo `{fixme}` references apply.",
  "references": "c3fb23486d904cc68a673463625fff919ad9886aff657a47f4a52c328a12be0c",
